msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:187
msgid "Whether to ask for confirmation when moving files to Trash"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:188
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo will ask for confirmation when you attempt to move "
"files to the Trash."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:192
msgid "Whether to ask for confirmation when deleting files, or emptying Trash"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:193
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo will ask for confirmation when you attempt to "
"delete files, or empty the Trash."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:197
msgid "Whether to enable immediate deletion"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:198
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo will have a feature allowing you to delete a file "
"immediately and in-place, instead of moving it to the trash. This feature "
"can be dangerous, so use caution."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:202
msgid "Whether to swap the hotkeys for Trash and Delete"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:203
msgid ""
"If set to true, the Delete key will permanently delete a file, and the Shift-"
"Delete key will only trash a file."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:208
msgid "When to show number of items in a folder"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:209
msgid ""
"Speed tradeoff for when to show the number of items in a folder. If set to "
"\"always\" then always show item counts, even if the folder is on a remote "
"server. If set to \"local-only\" then only show counts for local file "
"systems. If set to \"never\" then never bother to compute item counts."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:213
msgid "Type of click used to launch/open files"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:214
msgid ""
"Possible values are \"single\" to launch files on a single click, or "
"\"double\" to launch them on a double click."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:218
msgid "What to do with executable text files when activated"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:219
msgid ""
"What to do with executable text files when they are activated (single or "
"double clicked). Possible values are \"launch\" to launch them as programs, "
"\"ask\" to ask what to do via a dialog, and \"display\" to display them as "
"text files."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:223
msgid "Image viewer executables to pass sort order to"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:224
msgid ""
"When opening a single image with an application in this list, allow that "
"viewer to display other images in the current nemo view, in the presented "
"order (including searches). Other image viewers can be added, but are likely "
"to ignore the order. The viewer Exec line must accept a list of files "
"(either %U or %F)."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:228
msgid "Use extra mouse button events in Nemo' browser window"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:229
msgid ""
"For users with mice that have \"Forward\" and \"Back\" buttons, this key "
"will determine if any action is taken inside of Nemo when either is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:233
msgid "Mouse button to activate the \"Forward\" command in browser window"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:234
msgid ""
"For users with mice that have buttons for \"Forward\" and \"Back\", this key "
"will set which button activates the \"Forward\" command in a browser window. "
"Possible values range between 6 and 14."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:238
msgid "Mouse button to activate the \"Back\" command in browser window"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:239
msgid ""
"For users with mice that have buttons for \"Forward\" and \"Back\", this key "
"will set which button activates the \"Back\" command in a browser window. "
"Possible values range between 6 and 14."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:244
msgid "When to show thumbnails of image files"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:245
msgid ""
"Speed tradeoff for when to show an image file as a thumbnail. If set to "
"\"always\" then always thumbnail, even if the folder is on a remote server. "
"If set to \"local-only\" then only show thumbnails for local file systems. "
"If set to \"never\" then never bother to thumbnail images, just use a "
"generic icon."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:249
msgid "Inherit thumbnail visibility from parent"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:250
msgid ""
"If set, folders will inherit their thumbnail visibility from their parents"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:254
msgid "Maximum image size for thumbnailing"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:255
msgid ""
"Images over this size (in bytes) won't be thumbnailed. The purpose of this "
"setting is to avoid thumbnailing large images that may take a long time to "
"load or use lots of memory."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:260
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo lets you edit and display file permissions in a "
"more unix-like way, accessing some more esoteric options."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:264
msgid "Show folders first in windows"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:265
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo shows folders prior to showing files in the icon "
"and list views."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:269
msgid "Show favorites first in windows"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:270
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo shows favorites prior to other files in the icon "
"and list views."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:277
msgid "Default sort order"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:278
msgid ""
"The default sort-order for items in the icon view. Possible values are "
"\"name\", \"size\", \"type\" and \"mtime\"."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:282
msgid "Reverse sort order in new windows"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:283
msgid ""
"If true, files in new windows will be sorted in reverse order. ie, if sorted "
"by name, then instead of sorting the files from \"a\" to \"z\", they will be "
"sorted from \"z\" to \"a\"; if sorted by size, instead of being "
"incrementally they will be sorted decrementally."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:287
msgid "Nemo uses the users home folder as the desktop"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:288
msgid ""
"If set to true, then Nemo will use the user's home folder as the desktop. If "
"it is false, then it will use ~/Desktop as the desktop."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:292
msgid "Directory opened on an ordinary Files launch"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:293
msgid ""
"Local folder URI to open when Files is launched without an explicit path. "
"Empty uses Home. Does not change bookmarks, tabs or explicit paths."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:303
msgid "Default folder viewer"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:304
msgid ""
"When a folder is visited this viewer is used unless you have selected "
"another view for that particular folder. Possible values are \"list-view\", "
"\"icon-view\", \"compact-view\" and \"miller-columns-view\"."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:308
msgid "Update search results after typing"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:309
msgid ""
"Use a short delay after input before refreshing filename or content matches."
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:314
msgid "Instant search typing delay in milliseconds"
msgstr ""

#: libnemo-private/org.nemo.gschema.xml:315
msgid ""
"Debounce time for search updates while typing, when instant search is "
"enabled."
msgstr ""

